  <data name="DIYFFBPedalPlugin_TextScriptHelpNCalc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>NCalc. Variables: t (time in s), dt (0.002 s), prev (last value), phase (radians, from the frequency field), pi, and every SimHub property, e.g. [DataCorePlugin.GameData.Rpms]. Functions: Sin, Cos, Abs, Min, Max, Pow, Sqrt, if(cond, a, b).
Pedal values (force, travel, ...): SimHub &gt; Available properties, search "diy_ffb_pedal".
Example (engine, angle): frequency 10 + 30 * [DataCorePlugin.GameData.Rpms] / [DataCorePlugin.GameData.MaxRpm], script 0.03 * Sin(phase)
Vibrations above ~40 Hz are damped strongly by the pedal.
Example (ABS, angle): if([DataCorePlugin.GameData.ABSActive] &gt; 0, 0.06 * Sin(2 * pi * 25 * t), 0)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DIYFFBPedalPlugin_TextScriptHelpJs" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>JavaScript (ES5, like SimHub's JS formulas). The script is the body of a function(t, dt, prev, phase): use return. Properties: $prop('DataCorePlugin.GameData.Rpms'). root keeps values between calls (root.x = ...). Math.sin, Math.min, ...
Pedal values (force, travel, ...): SimHub &gt; Available properties, search "diy_ffb_pedal".
Runs 500 times per second: keep it short, no loops over large data. 'CPU' shows the cost (10 ms/s = 1 % of a core).
Example (lockup steps): var l = $prop('ShakeITMotorsV3Plugin.Export.wheelsliplock.All'); var a = l &gt;= 20 ? 0.8 : l &gt;= 10 ? 0.3 : 0; return 0.06 * a * Math.sin(2 * pi * 30 * t);</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DIYFFBPedalPlugin_TextScriptDangerTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>DANGER: robot mode!</value>
  </data>
  <data name="DIYFFBPedalPlugin_TextScriptDangerText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>With scripts I move the pedal on my own. I can push your foot and put energy into it instead of only reacting to it. A wrong sign, unit or typo can mean full force or a hard kick. Start with small values and gain 1, keep your foot on the pedal when testing, and disable the script at the first surprise.</value>
  </data>
